{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: vectorized the repeated `beta[n] ~ multi_normal(...)` prior into the single top-level statement `beta ~ multi_normal(...)`, and vectorized the elementwise normal observation model into the single protected-data statement `y ~ normal(eta, sigma_y)` using a deterministic local mean array `eta`. This removes sampling statements from loops and gives protected data a plain top-level left-hand side without changing the posterior density. No data changes were required; `data_safe.json` is the supplied data.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> T;
  array[T] real x;
  real xbar;
  array[N, T] real y;
  cov_matrix[2] Omega;
}
parameters {
  array[N] vector[2] beta;
  vector[2] mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigmasq_y;
  cov_matrix[2] Sigma_beta;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  sigma_y = sqrt(sigmasq_y);
}
model {
  array[N, T] real eta;

  sigmasq_y ~ inv_gamma(0.001, 0.001);
  mu_beta ~ normal(0, 100);
  Sigma_beta ~ inv_wishart(2, Omega);
  beta ~ multi_normal(mu_beta, Sigma_beta);

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    for (t in 1 : T) {
      eta[n, t] = beta[n, 1] + beta[n, 2] * x[t];
    }
  }
  y ~ normal(eta, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"T":2,"x":[4.722043915562804,5.9159396310582935],"xbar":6.618859819725233,"y":[[3.0,3.0],[3.0,3.0],[3.0,3.0]],"Omega":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
